  "id": "Compound::DB00475 - Gene::2556",
  "verbalization": "Chlordiazepoxide is likely to interact with Gabra3 through a mechanism involving GABA receptor activity. The evidence suggests that Chlordiazepoxide binds to Gabra2 or Gabrg2, which then participates in GABA receptor activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Gabra3, indicating a potential role in the regulation of GABA receptor function. The overlapping pathways highlight a shared involvement in benzodiazepine receptor activity, suggesting that Chlordiazepoxide may influence GABA receptor function through a common intermediary. The integration of these pathways implies that Chlordiazepoxide could modulate Gabra3 through a GABA receptor-mediated mechanism, possibly by affecting the functional state of Gabra3 in response to GABA signaling.",
